\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A partial exchange in a nearest-neighbor hop}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let the group of order two act on an orthonormal triple
#{e_1,e_2,e_3} by the respective signs #{+,-,+} at its
nonidentity element. Take #{V_+} spanned by #{e_1,e_2} and
#{V_-} spanned by #{e_3}. Define the value coefficient #{b}
to exchange #{e_1} with #{e_3} and to kill #{e_2}. Its
two nonzero entries pair equal group characters in opposite
sectors. Thus #{b} commutes with the group, is odd and is
self-adjoint by \ref{fdip-018K}. Its kernel is the sign line.
The two sectors have different dimensions.}

\p{On a circle of period at least three with identity links,
let #{T_1} shift a field one site forward. The hop
#{H=(T_1+T_1^{-1})b} acts by
##{(H\psi)(x)=b\psi(x+1)+b\psi(x-1).}
The two shifts are adjoints and the constant #{b} commutes
with them. Thus #{H} is a self-adjoint nearest-neighbor hop
commuting with the constant group action and exchanging signs
where it has nonzero image. On a constant field with value
#{e_1} its value is #{2e_3}, while every field in the sign
line is killed. This hop uses only the shared trivial
summands.}
